{
  "id": "9fd13277-37ee-4962-ac71-5f752dd71934",
  "productId": "openmrs",
  "title": "Patient Bill Payment Flow",
  "updatedAt": 1793522566275,
  "answers": [
    {
      "id": "S2Y0olducsadJR3g",
      "productId": "openmrs",
      "question": "When a cashier records a payment for a patient bill in the billing app, what happens from the button click in the UI down to the database write? Walk me through it.",
      "generation": "g-ab363e",
      "kind": "partial",
      "paragraphs": [
        {
          "text": "Here is the whole path, from the \"Process Payment\" button to the `saveOrUpdate` that writes the row.",
          "citations": []
        },
        {
          "text": "## 1. The button in the UI",
          "citations": []
        },
        {
          "text": "- The button itself is rendered in `payments.component.tsx`; it calls `handleProcessPayment` on click and is disabled unless a method and amount are present and the form is valid [1].\n- The form fields (method / amount / reference) are Carbon controls bound by react-hook-form through `Controller` in `PaymentForm` [2]. Payment method options come from `usePaymentModes`, which GETs `.../billing/paymentMode` [3].",
          "citations": [
            1,
            2,
            3
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "## 2. Validation and the submit handler",
          "citations": []
        },
        {
          "text": "- The form is validated with a Zod schema: method is required, amount must be positive and may not exceed `netAmount - tenderedAmount` (amount due) [4]. Amount due is computed as `netAmount - tenderedAmount` [5].\n- `handleProcessPayment` guards on method/amount, then calls `processBillPayment` with `{ instanceType: method, amountTendered, amount: bill.totalAmount }` and the bill UUID [6]. The payload shape is `PaymentRequestPayload` [7].\n- On success it shows a snackbar, clears the visit's \"pending payment\" attribute via `updateBillVisitAttribute` [8], resets the form, and revalidates the bill and patient-payment-status SWR caches. On failure it shows an error snackbar [9].",
          "citations": [
            4,
            5,
            6,
            7,
            8,
            9
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "## 3. The HTTP call",
          "citations": []
        },
        {
          "text": "- `processBillPayment` POSTs the JSON payload to `${restBaseUrl}/billing/bill/{billUuid}/payment` [10]; `apiBasePath` is `${restBaseUrl}/billing/` [11].",
          "citations": [
            10,
            11
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "## 4. The REST layer (module)",
          "citations": []
        },
        {
          "text": "- The URL maps to `PaymentResource`, declared as a `@SubResource` of `BillResource` with path `payment` [12].\n- The Web Services REST framework resolves the parent bill from `{billUuid}` and sets it via `setParent` (`instance.setBill(parent)`) and `newDelegate()` (a fresh `Payment`) omod/src/main/java/org/openmrs/module/billing/web/rest/resource/PaymentResource.java.\n- Incoming JSON properties are bound through `@PropertySetter` methods: `instanceType` → looks up the `PaymentMode` by UUID and sets it omod/src/main/java/org/openmrs/module/billing/web/rest/resource/PaymentResource.java; `amount` and `amountTendered` → `BigDecimal` on the `Payment` omod/src/main/java/org/openmrs/module/billing/web/rest/resource/PaymentResource.java; `cashier` → resolved to a `Provider` omod/src/main/java/org/openmrs/module/billing/web/rest/resource/PaymentResource.java.",
          "citations": [
            12
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "## 5. save() and the service call",
          "citations": []
        },
        {
          "text": "- `PaymentResource.save` defaults the cashier to the current provider if none was set (throwing if the user has no provider), then attaches the payment to the bill with `bill.addPayment(delegate)` and calls `BillService.saveBill(bill)` omod/src/main/java/org/openmrs/module/billing/web/rest/resource/PaymentResource.java.\n- `Bill.addPayment` adds the payment to the bill's payment set, sets the back-reference `payment.setBill(this)`, and calls `synchronizeBillStatus()` api/src/main/java/org/openmrs/module/billing/api/model/Bill.java.\n- `synchronizeBillStatus` compares `getTotalPayments()` with `getAmountAfterDiscount()`: if fully settled it sets the bill (and its paid line items) to `PAID`, otherwise to `POSTED`; it refuses to touch refund states, and stays `POSTED` if discount drift is detected api/src/main/java/org/openmrs/module/billing/api/model/Bill.java.",
          "citations": []
        },
        {
          "text": "## 6. Persistence",
          "citations": []
        },
        {
          "text": "- `BillServiceImpl.saveBill` is `@Transactional` and delegates to the DAO api/src/main/java/org/openmrs/module/billing/api/impl/BillServiceImpl.java.\n- `HibernateBillDAO.saveBill` performs the actual database write: `sessionFactory.getCurrentSession().saveOrUpdate(bill)` api/src/main/java/org/openmrs/module/billing/api/db/hibernate/HibernateBillDAO.java. Because the `Payment` is now a child in the bill's cascade-managed collection, Hibernate inserts the payment row (and updates the bill's status) when the transaction commits.",
          "citations": []
        },
        {
          "text": "## Flow at a glance",
          "citations": []
        },
        {
          "text": "```mermaid\n---\ntitle: Payment recording flow\n---\nflowchart TD\n  btn[\"Process Payment button\"] --> submit[\"handleProcessPayment\"]\n  submit --> zod[\"Zod validation\"]\n  zod --> resource[\"processBillPayment\"]\n  resource --> post[\"POST billing/bill/uuid/payment\"]\n  post --> rest[\"PaymentResource save\"]\n  rest --> add[\"Bill.addPayment\"]\n  add --> status[\"synchronizeBillStatus\"]\n  rest --> svc[\"BillServiceImpl.saveBill\"]\n  svc --> dao[\"HibernateBillDAO.saveBill\"]\n  dao --> db[\"session.saveOrUpdate\"]\n```",
          "citations": []
        },
        {
          "text": "A couple of details worth noting: the frontend sends only `instanceType`, `amountTendered` and `amount` (the full bill top-up), so the per-payment `amount` is replaced with `bill.totalAmount` rather than the amount the cashier typed src/invoice/payments/payments.component.tsx; and bill-level status changes (`PAID`/`POSTED`) are a side effect of `addPayment`, not of a separate status endpoint.",
          "citations": []
        }
      ],
